NAME
       cp - copy files and directories

SYNOPSIS
       cp [-fiprRv] source ... target

DESCRIPTION
       Copies SOURCE to TARGET, or several SOURCEs into a directory.
       Copying a directory requires -R.

OPTIONS
       -f     overwrite an existing target without asking
       -i     ask before overwriting an existing target
       -p     preserve attributes (accepted, currently has no effect)
       -R, -r copy directories recursively
       -v     print each file as it is copied

EXAMPLES
       cp notes.txt /mnt/backup/
       cp -Rv /usr/share/media /mnt/media

SEE ALSO
       mv(1), rm(1), ln(1)
